IDEA: HCAUDIT-SID
TITLE: Null-calibrated hyperbolic contrast audit that repairs at most five percent of SID assignments inside a measured prefix guard
MOTIVATION: SHAPE (A). Three rounds moved the many (curved residual 0.05439; global geodesic pull of 99.1% of items 0.05165; global extra PPMI level 0.04823) and lost monotonically with distance from the plain text geometry, not with prefix count. Behaviour CONTRAST is the only diagnostic that predicts recall (+0.7104 plain, +0.7170 Euclidean control) while Gromov-delta weighting and ancestor-depth weighting hurt (+0.12, +0.075 wrongly signed). So this mechanism freezes the encoder, adds no level, pulls nothing to a barycentre, uses no Gromov delta and no ancestor depth, and repairs only the statistically demonstrable tail where text geometry and behaviour contrast disagree, with the level-1 and per-level prefix drift measured and bounded.
NOVELTY: Unlike round 1 (curved residual chain), round 2 (global popularity-adjusted successor barycentre), round 3 (extra PPMI-direction level pinned by argmin), poincare-frechet-successor-codebook (successor-weighted Frechet codebook), CURVCTRL-SID (level curvature from prefix-transition score) and BRad-RQ (behaviour-ranked radial assignment), this never re-ranks or moves the bulk. It audits at most 5% of the 24556 items, the eligible set is fixed by a degree-stratified permutation null on behaviour contrast, the target codeword is chosen inside one Lorentzian score containing both behaviour affinity and curved distance, the budget is emergent from the null, the guard is measured, and curvature is treated as a gauge fixed by a data quantile (nothing to tune).
CHANGE: At the end of frozen Stage 2, build train-only successor-PPMI profiles, select items whose contrast with their level-1 subtree is significant under a degree-conserving permutation null, and re-quantize only those items (<=5% of 24556) with one score: z-scored behaviour affinity to the candidate subtree profile minus z-scored Lorentz distance to the candidate cumulative reconstruction, under a checked and reported prefix guard.
SPECIFICATION: N=24556, L=4, K codebook size per level; h_i frozen Stage-2 encoder output; e(l,k) level-l codebook vector; c(i,l) baseline codeword; r(i,l)=sum_{m<=l} e(m,c(i,m)). From TRAIN sequences only: successor counts N_ij, top-50 PPMI vectors b_i (L2), subtree profiles beta(l,k)=L2(mean_{j:prefix_l(j)=k} b_j). Eligibility g_i=max_{k!=c(i,1)} cos(b_i,beta(1,k))-cos(b_i,beta(1,c(i,1))); null = 20 permutations of b inside outgoing-degree deciles; tau = 99.5th percentile of pooled null g (documented 0.5% false-positive convention); eligible iff g_i>tau and total behavioural degree d_i>=20. Rank by d_i*g_i descending, B_max=floor(0.05N). Curvature gauge c0=1/q99({||h_i||} U {||e(l,k)||})^2 (99th percentile maps to hyperbolic radius 1). Map x~=exp_0^{c0}(x). Score s(i,l,k)=zhat_k[cos(b_i,beta(l,k))]-zhat_k[d_{c0}(x~(h_i),x~(r(i,l-1)+e(l,k)))/R_l], R_l = median baseline d_{c0}(x~(h_i),x~(r(i,l))) floored at 1e-3, zhat per-item z-score over k with sigma floor 1e-6. For a selected item greedy l=1..L: k*=argmax_{k used} s(i,l,k); flip only if s(i,l,k*)>s(i,l,c(i,l)); else keep baseline codeword and residual. Guard: level-1 count total variation <=0.05; distinct used prefix counts each level within +/-5% of baseline; changed level-1 tokens <=0.05N. On failure drop the lowest d_i*g_i item and recompute (<=B_max times). Export repaired SID table to the frozen Stage-3 protocol.
COST: Per training step at the frozen scale: 0 added work; 24 steps/epoch x 3000 epochs unchanged at 0.145-0.16 s/epoch (435-480 s). Audit once at export: 4*N*K <= 1.0e8 score evaluations after 24556+4K exp maps and 4K subtree profiles, about 1-10 GPU-seconds (1-2 CPU-minutes), under 0.2% of Stage-2 wall clock; guard bisection <=1227 histogram recomputations; Stage 3 unchanged. Total added wall clock under 1 minute.` ;
await tools.progress.append_progress({content: p1});
return "p1 ok";

